## Fixed normal CLI evidence and its precise limit

Retained PartB receipts1/2 (`f01852479fb7a07d8f514a7b52b5715956c279dde90e92f45457cb1468bbf3c3`, `0b1726ec50b36f1298080cc6b4a413eca77382eb28ff0ddf6ea423d45ff8a1f4`) show four exact normal `merge drain --json` invocations of debug/thegn SHA205941c3b3b0f9b19e7743eb7beed9d117e428dd0554d92be36b5a3934b03918. All exit0, leaders reaped, no retained/identity-lost cleanup, private roots removed. The combined focused receipt ties tested Rust to frozen623 while explicitly declining an independently retained embedded623 version claim. Canonical's diagnostic source files still match that reviewed source. `cmd/merge.rs:634` calls the same `merge_driver::drive_queue`, which directly delegates to the tested driver mapping at148–183.

Those actual CLI fixtures seed stale result/conflict/error values, generate real conflict/red-gate cases, then assert an isolation-held row has no resultOID/conflict_paths and exactly the hold error; a later plain drain recovers the same row to ready. They are useful fixed-normal-binary route and stale-clearing evidence. Their terminal first result is **agent_blocked**, not deferred or gate_error. Exact deferred conflict-path SQL placement is proved by the separate shipping-driver/SQLite fixture; actual gate_error field placement is proved through the native authenticated transport fixture. No one retained normal-CLI receipt covers every diagnostic variant. This layered scope is sufficient for the described existing mapping bug; do not rewrite the PartB historical receipt as having claimed whole THE608 at the time.

If the primary reviewer interprets the shared historical fixed-CLI checkbox as demanding one additional normal-CLI terminal-deferred SQL specimen, the smallest optional acceptance-only addition is the already-owned PartB fixture with conflict_handoff=notify and autoland/cleanup disabled, asserting exact conflict.txt in paths and null error/result against the actual drain. It would need a reviewed fixture and root-run gate; no production fix or live resource is needed. I do not infer that extra end-to-end variant as mandatory from THE608's explicit focused private-SQLite criterion.

